 - `npm run dev` starts Vite at `http://127.0.0.1:5173/Tahion_Personal_site/`.
 - `npm run preview` serves the production build at `http://127.0.0.1:4173/Tahion_Personal_site/`.
 - `npm run check` runs ESLint, Prettier check, TypeScript, and production build.
+- `npm test` runs the built-in Node test runner for the visual preference contract.
+
+## Visual Preferences
+
+The background variant and color theme are stored together as a versioned JSON record under `tahion.visual.preferences`:
+
+```json
+{ "version": 1, "variant": "signal", "theme": "acid" }
+```
+
+On first load, a missing record reads the legacy raw-string keys `tahion.backdrop.variant` and `tahion.backdrop.theme` independently. Any valid legacy choice is migrated into the combined record; legacy keys are never removed or rewritten. Missing or invalid values use `signal` and `acid`. A malformed, unsupported, or unknown-version current record is left untouched and uses both defaults.
+
+Changes in another tab are applied from same-origin `localStorage` storage events. Valid records update both controls and the backdrop, while removing the combined key resets both defaults. Storage failures are ignored so the controls continue to work in memory.
 
